    "raw_text": "EXAMPLE DEFENCE RESEARCH LABORATORY (FICTIONAL)\nAdvertisement No. EDRL/RECT/2026/07\nFilling up of one post of Scientist 'E' (Avionics and Sensor Systems) on deputation basis.\n\nEssential Qualifications:\n1. Master's degree in Electronics / Electronics and Communication / Avionics Engineering from a recognised university.\n2. At least 10 years of experience in design, integration or testing of avionics, embedded or sensor systems.\n\nDesirable:\n1. Ph.D. in Electronics, Electrical or Computer Engineering.\n2. Experience in machine learning, computer vision or edge AI deployment for airborne or UAV platforms.\n3. Publications in peer-reviewed journals.\n4. Experience of leading technical teams and project coordination.\n\nDuties:\nDesign and evaluation of airborne sensor and avionics subsystems; development of embedded processing for UAV payloads; preparation of technical specifications and test plans; guidance of junior scientists.\n\nEligibility:\nOfficers of the Central Government holding analogous posts on a regular basis, or with 5 years of regular service in Level 11. Age not exceeding 56 years on the closing date.\n\nDocuments to be enclosed:\nBio-data in the prescribed proforma, copies of APAR for the last five years, vigilance clearance, integrity certificate and no-objection certificate from the parent department.\n",
